Future note: we discussed this with @TimoBakx during the SymfonyCon hackday.
Another idea we had was to trigger one event per controller attribute, before the `kernel.response` event.
The main benefit would be true lazy loading. This would work around a too common issue in Symfony apps: listeners that do nothing most of the time but are still loaded (together with their deps - something we might also improve by making listeners lazy by default, since this is much cheaper with native lazy objects).
This note shouldn't prevent this PR from being considered (quite the contrary to me).
